class:: RippleFormantOsc
summary:: Cycle-synchronous decaying formant ripples
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/NovelOscillators

description::

RippleFormantOsc launches two independent exponentially decaying sinusoidal
ripples at every wrap of a base oscillator. Each ripple integrates an
exponential frequency sweep, so its formant can rise or fall coherently during
the base cycle. Optional oversampling and Nyquist fades limit aliasing.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/Formant::. Both create a pitched
source with formant emphasis, but RippleFormantOsc exposes two explicitly
cycle-synchronous, chirped ripple components and their reconstruction.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Signed base-cycle frequency in hertz. Negative values reverse base and ripple
phase while retaining coherent resets.

argument:: formantA
Initial frequency of ripple A in hertz.

argument:: formantB
Initial frequency of ripple B in hertz.

argument:: decayA
Exponential time constant for ripple A in seconds.

argument:: decayB
Exponential time constant for ripple B in seconds.

argument:: sweepA
Ripple A frequency movement in octaves across one base cycle, clamped to
code::-8..8::.

argument:: sweepB
Ripple B frequency movement in octaves across one base cycle.

argument:: balance
Equal-power position between ripple A and B, clamped to code::0..1::.

argument:: baseLevel
Base sine gain in the mixed output.

argument:: rippleLevel
Combined ripple gain in the mixed output.

argument:: phase
Base readout phase in radians.

argument:: oversample
Initialization-rate factor code::1::, code::2::, or code::4::.

argument:: mul
Multiplier applied to all four outputs.

argument:: add
Offset added to all four outputs after multiplication.

returns::
Four sample-coherent signals: base, ripple A, ripple B, and the documented
level-and-balance mix.

method:: kr

RippleFormantOsc is audio-rate only. This method throws an error.

subsection:: Discussion

Ripple phase is integrated from instantaneous frequency rather than
interpolated directly. Evaluation stops after the exponential envelope falls
below a negligible threshold and starts again on the next base wrap.

examples::

code::
(
{ RippleFormantOsc.ar(80, 700, 1300)[3] * 0.07 }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
    var signal = RippleFormantOsc.ar(
        48, 430, 1900, 0.025, 0.006,
        sweepA: 1.3, sweepB: -0.8,
        balance: LFTri.kr(0.08).range(0, 1),
        oversample: 4
    );
    Splay.ar([signal[1], signal[2]]) * 0.055;
}.play;
)
::

